ercent": 70.1, "maxFar": 1.5}, {"district": "R6", "sharePercent": 29.9, "maxFar": 3.9}], "checks": ["Split zoning lot: R4 on 70.1% (FAR 1.5), R6 on 29.9% (FAR 3.9) by the city's zoning map. The floor area ratio is the area-weighted 2.218 and may be placed anywhere on the lot (ZR 77-22); each portion keeps its own district's yards, heights and setbacks (ZR 77-27, 77-28); dwelling units are summed by portion (ZR 77-25) and residential parking weighted by area (ZR 77-321). The planning engine draws the mapped boundary; a lot that existed on December 15, 1961 may extend one district up to 25 ft across it (ZR 77-211).", "R4: Corner lot: no rear yard is drawn within the corner portion, within 100 ft of each intersecting street line (ZR 12-10, ZR 23-344); beyond it the rear yard is kept along the lines facing the rear. A side lot line beyond 100 ft of the street it meets counts as a rear lot line (ZR 23-344), which needs only a 5 ft yard where it meets an adjoining side lot line; the tax map does not say which, so the yard is kept. The planning engine checks the 135 degree angle on the lot polygon.", "R4: Corner lot: one front yard may be 5 ft shallower than the table (ZR 23-321); both are drawn at full depth.", "R4: Qualifying residential site assumed (ZR 12-10): 1.5 FAR, any residence type and the ZR 23-424 heights. Confirm the lot meets the definition (transit zone, lot size and frontage, existing community facility floor space, or qualifying senior housing).", "R6: Rear yard drawn as 20 ft up to 75 ft of height and 30 ft above, as curated from ZR 23-342; verify against the current text before relying on it.", "R6: Corner lot: no rear yard is drawn within the corner portion, within 100 ft of each intersecting street line (ZR 12-10, ZR 23-344); beyond it the rear yard is kept along the lines facing the rear. A side lot line beyond 100 ft of the street it meets counts as a rear lot line (ZR 23-344), which needs no rear yard where it meets an adjoining side lot line; the tax map does not say which, so the yard is kept. The planning engine checks the 135 degree angle on the lot polygon.", "R6: The 97.2% of the lot within 100 ft of a wide street takes the wide-street heights (base 40 to 65 ft, building 95 ft) and the rest the narrow-street heights (base 30 to 65 ft, building 85 ft) (ZR 23-432 notes 1 and 2, ZR 77-28).", "R6: Court minimums (ZR 23-352 inner courts, 23-353 outer courts) are reported in controls.courts and not carved from the drawn envelope; which courts a design needs depends on where legally required windows face."]}}